{"resourceIdentifier":"2072","resourceName":"UK CowCredit project: A UK dairy initiative to reduce methane from enteric fermentation","description":"The UK CowCredit project (Multiple Instances of Project Activities) aims to involve the UK dairy industry with the purpose to reduce greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions from the livestock sector. The project activity introduces Mootral® natural feed supplement into dairy cattle diet aiming to reduce methane (CH4) emissions from enteric fermentation by direct inhibition of methanogens in the rumen. This process results in a substantial net reduction of GHG emissions, because of the avoidance of CH4 released into the atmosphere, which would occur under normal operating circumstances (“the business as usual”). Over the 10 years of the first crediting period, the project will generate an estimated annual average reduction of 187'563 tons of carbon dioxide equivalent (tCO2e).PUBLIC COMMENT PERIOD:This project was open for public comment from 06 December 2019 – 05 January 2020. No comments were received.","location":{"latitude":55.370000,"longitude":-3.600000},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2072"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Lancashire county"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"MOOTRAL SA"},{"type":"string","value":"Switzerland"},{"type":"string","value":"0041 79 827 9335"},{"type":"string","value":"cgirard@mootral.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2072"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"187563"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Livestock, enteric fermentation, and manure management"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type